+dragonrage-vulkan.patch is an altered version, authored for this Dragon Rage fork
+with Codex assistance. It is not an official SDL change or an upstream contribution.
+SDL's original copyright/license notice is preserved. The added observation code
+is available under the same Zlib license.
+
+The optional creation property dragonrage.vulkan.probe enables observation for
+BT3 only. Without it, command ordering, features and extension requirements remain
+unchanged. BT4 does not set the property. No new public SDL API is exported.
+
+The patch observes real vkQueueSubmit/vkQueuePresentKHR results, signalled
+submission fences, optional Vulkan timestamp queries, and optional
+VK_GOOGLE_display_timing feedback. It does not replace SDL resource transitions,
+queue ownership, semaphores, command-buffer recycling or presentation logic.
+GOOGLE_display_timing is enumerated before being enabled and is never required.
+
+Core query pools are allocated once per used command buffer, capped at 64 query
+slots; queries never use WAIT_BIT. No query/present polling creates allocations
+per image. Driver feedback and GPU timestamp availability are reported separately.
+
+Build instructions and acceptance limits are in docs/AUDITORIA-opt6.md in the
+Dragon-ball-rage overlay repository. apply_sdl_probe.py verifies the original
+backend's SHA before applying this patch.
